---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Linux Filesystem Hierarchy — Interactive Algorithms">
  <h1>Linux Filesystem Hierarchy</h1>
  <p class="desc">
    Unix systems put everything under a single root, <code>/</code>, and the Filesystem Hierarchy
    Standard defines what belongs where. Browse the tree, search for a file or purpose, or filter by
    the two axes the standard cares about: static vs. variable, and shareable vs. unshareable.
  </p>

  <div class="fs-root">
    <div class="viz-controls">
      <input class="fs-search" type="search" placeholder="Search paths, purposes, contents…" />
      <button class="fs-expand">Expand all</button>
      <button class="fs-collapse">Collapse</button>
      <span class="fs-count"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="chip-row fs-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter directories">
      <button class="chip active" data-filter="all">all</button>
      <button class="chip" data-filter="static">static</button>
      <button class="chip" data-filter="variable">variable</button>
      <button class="chip" data-filter="shareable">shareable</button>
      <button class="chip" data-filter="unshareable">unshareable</button>
    </div>

    <div class="fs-cols">
      <div class="fs-tree" role="tree" aria-label="Filesystem hierarchy"></div>
      <aside class="fs-detail">
        <div class="fs-crumb"></div>
        <p class="fs-summary-text"></p>
        <div class="fs-chips"></div>
        <p class="fs-detail-text"></p>
        <p class="fs-spec hidden"></p>
        <div class="fs-examples"></div>
      </aside>
    </div>
    <p class="raid-hint">
      Click a directory to expand and inspect it; arrow keys navigate the tree.
    </p>

    <h2>Why the split exists</h2>
    <p class="desc">
      FHS separates files along two axes so they can live on different filesystems: static files can
      sit on read-only media, and shareable files can be served to several hosts at once. The
      standard gives this example layout:
    </p>
    <table class="complexity fs-matrix">
      <thead>
        <tr><th></th><th>shareable</th><th>unshareable</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>static</th><td><code>/usr</code>, <code>/opt</code></td><td><code>/etc</code>, <code>/boot</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th>variable</th><td><code>/var/mail</code>, <code>/var/spool/news</code></td><td><code>/var/run</code>, <code>/var/lock</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="raid-hint">Source: Filesystem Hierarchy Standard 3.0, §2.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  import { initFilesystem } from '../../scripts/filesystem';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.fs-root').forEach(initFilesystem);
</script>
